maps.summary:
Claims live per lesson in src/demos/<domain>/<slug>/meta.json under `claims[]`. Each claim has id (the "address", <domain>.<slug>.c<n>), text, support, source and status, and optionally checkedBy/checkedOn/note. Two pieces of code in the protected tools/company.mjs judge them. cmdCheck validates the schema (lines 383-390). claimGates (lines 303-321) sets the publish floor: every claim must be verified or withdrawn, every verified claim needs checkedBy and checkedOn, and checkedBy must not equal owner.builder. The fact-checker role (company/roles/fact-checker.md, .claude/agents/fact-checker.md) changes status by editing meta.json by hand. It writes company/reviews/<slug>/<date>-fact-check.md and must read the walkthrough transcript first. No hook or CLI verb carries out a claim transition, and the independence rule compares two role-name strings, not identities.

Meta can run this as a flow's `check` stage. The signer level is `checker`, filled by a fact-checker role. Meta's engine already refuses a check signed by the order's builder (lib.mjs:377 and :504). For evidence, the checker leaves the room with `--evidence=company/reviews/<slug>/<date>-fact-check.md` plus the edited meta.json. Meta has no adapter for most of what the stage needs:
- a per-lesson claim gate that code can run (test1 today runs only node --test files or the text checks, state.mjs:264);
- a way to confirm that the checker changed only status fields;
- a "held" outcome for claims a blocked host stops, besides pass/revise;
- signer identity written into checkedBy from the room's run, rather than typed in by the agent.

`company check` cannot be used as a stage gate as it stands. It is company-wide and exits 1 right now (811 errors). `company claims --open` is human-readable text that always exits 0.
